<%# The answer to a write that waited past the SQLite busy timeout (ApplicationController).

    No layout and no record: the database is busy, so this page asks it nothing (the layout's
    masthead does, to name the visitor). It links the application stylesheet, which Propshaft
    resolves without a query, and uses its classes rather than inline styles, which the
    content security policy would refuse anyway. %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <title>The server was busy</title>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag "application" %>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main id="main" class="page">
      <h1>The server was busy for a moment</h1>
      <p>
        Another write held the database longer than we wait for it, so
        <strong>your action was not applied</strong> and nothing was changed. Nothing is lost:
        go back and try it again in a few seconds.
      </p>
      <p><%= link_to "Back to the home page", root_path %></p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
